{"equalOutcomes": true, "outcomes": ["\u2714 selectTemplate resolves a coding-domain input to the skill-pointer template, for any kind/tier (mechanical table lookup, keyed on domain)", "\u2714 selectTemplate resolves even with no arguments at all \u2014 an absent domain folds to \"coding\", which resolves to the skill-pointer template", "\u2714 selectTemplate folds an unrecognized domain string to \"coding\" too (same fold as undefined, not a fall-back to the old default)", "\u2714 selectTemplate still resolves a real registered non-coding domain (\"synthetic\") to the default template \u2014 the wildcard fallback survives for domains that exist but are not \"coding\"", "\u2714 selectTemplate resolves a coding-domain, stage:\"discovery\" input to the discovery template instead of the skill-pointer one", "\u2714 selectTemplate omitting stage entirely (every pre-tsk-5mj call site) still resolves to the skill-pointer template, byte-identical to before", "\u2714 selectTemplate with stage:\"discovery\" on a non-coding domain still falls through to that domain's own rule (stage only narrows the coding rule)", "\u2714 loadTemplate reads worker-prompt-default.txt from TEMPLATE_DIR and it contains the eight named placeholders", "\u2714 renderTemplate(worker-prompt-default.txt, ...) golden output \u2014 no-feedback shape, byte-for-byte", "\u2714 renderTemplate golden output \u2014 with-feedback shape includes the Human feedback section verbatim", "\u2714 renderTemplate(worker-prompt-skill-pointer.txt, ...) golden output \u2014 no-feedback shape, byte-for-byte", "\u2714 hashTemplate returns a stable 64-hex-char sha256 digest for the same template across repeated calls", "\u2139 tests 12", "\u2139 pass 12", "\u2139 fail 0", "\u2139 cancelled 0", "\u2139 skipped 0", "\u2139 todo 0"]}
